-- title:
--   Exact finite data for an8000-shift prime-pair certificate
-- statement:
--   The data consist of the first8000 odd primes, from3 through81817, the rational weight $K(m)=\prod_{p\mid m,\ p>2}(p-1)/(p-2)$, its rounded weight $\lceil10000K(m)\rceil$, and a fixed16-bit lookup table indexed by half-differences below40909. The table is intended for a finite-shift second moment argument. Its comparison with the rational rounded weights and its total pair sum are separate theorem obligations; these definitions do not assert either certificate.
-- source:
--   Exact finite data generated for the known Riesel-Vaughan prime-sum method. Encoding adapted from public Prove2Me definition OAI_OddGoldbach23_CertificateData; this variant uses8000 shifts, scale10000 and half-difference indices. Context: Riesel and Vaughan, On sums of primes (1983).

